@startuml sequence
title Auth0 login to AWS S3 with Workload Identity Federation

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9B458

actor User
participant "SPA\n(browser)" as SPA
participant "Auth0\n(custom domain)" as Auth0
participant "AWS STS" as STS
participant "Amazon S3" as S3

== 1. Log in with Auth0 ==
User -> SPA : Open the app
User -> SPA : Click "Log in with Auth0"
SPA -> Auth0 : GET /authorize\n(client_id = SPA, audience = API, PKCE challenge)
Auth0 -> User : Login page
User -> Auth0 : Credentials
Auth0 --> SPA : Redirect back with ?code=...
SPA -> Auth0 : POST /oauth/token (code + PKCE verifier)
Auth0 --> SPA : Access token (JWT)
note right of Auth0
  iss = https://<custom domain>/
  aud = [API audience, /userinfo]
  azp = SPA client ID
  sub = auth0|<user id>
end note

== 2. Exchange the token for temporary AWS credentials ==
SPA -> STS : AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\n(RoleArn, WebIdentityToken = access token)\n**unsigned: no AWS credentials in the browser**
STS -> Auth0 : Fetch OIDC discovery + JWKS\n(from the IAM OIDC provider's issuer URL)
Auth0 --> STS : Signing keys
note over STS
  Role trust policy checks:
  1. signature and iss match the IAM OIDC provider
  2. azp (as aud) is a registered client ID
  3. oaud contains the API audience
     (rejects ID tokens and tokens for other APIs)
end note
STS --> SPA : Temporary credentials (access key, secret, session token)\n+ SubjectFromWebIdentityToken

== 3. Use S3 with the temporary credentials ==
SPA -> S3 : ListObjectsV2, prefix = users/<sub>/\n(SigV4 signed with the temporary credentials)
S3 --> SPA : Your objects
User -> SPA : Choose a file and upload
SPA -> S3 : PutObject users/<sub>/<file>
S3 --> SPA : 200 OK
note over S3
  Role permissions policy limits every request
  to users/${issuer:sub}/* , so one role serves all users.
end note
SPA -> S3 : List or get under another user's prefix
S3 --> SPA : 403 AccessDenied

== 4. Credentials expire ==
SPA -> Auth0 : getTokenSilently() when the credentials are within 5 minutes of expiry
Auth0 --> SPA : New access token
SPA -> STS : AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (as in step 2)

@enduml
